  "review_notes": [
    "The *with* of *daubed ... with untempered mortar* is the preposition through which the English verb reaches its bare Hebrew object, and joins the verb's unit as the same construction does at 22.7, 22.12, 22.26 and 22.30; the object noun keeps only *untempered mortar*.",
    "No object marker and no Hebrew preposition stands on תָּפֵל, so no present morpheme competes for the word under rules 16 and 11."
